    "The PSREQ framework has been developed to address the limitations of current antiviral and therapeutic strategies. Conventional approaches often rely on therapies that target singular viral mechanisms or transient stages of infection, leaving room for viral resistance, incomplete suppression, and persistent latency. In contrast, the PSREQ Pathway integrates three complementary mechanisms—targeted molecular binding, ionic stabilization, and systemic disruption of viral replication and assembly processes. This multifaceted approach ensures adaptability, durability, and precision in addressing viral pathogenesis while minimizing the risk of resistance.\n",
